In article <2378@trlluna.trl.oz> simon@shiva.trl.oz (Simon Michnowicz - A Free Spirit) writes:
>I have just come across what appears to be a bug in
>pl9.  I have been playing the game in "discover" mode,
>and my polymorphed character was saved as 310<new_name>.Z,
>not 310<my_name>.Z.  Hence I could not start the game up again.
>I copied the files over, but wonder if this is a bug or not? 

This isn't a bug, and it's not exclusive to discover mode.  Instead,
it is a feature that allows players to have more than one character 
at the same time (a bane to us games administrators).  Anyways, in order
to retrieve the character, just type 'nethack -u<name>' where <name> is
the name of the character (in this case new_name).  This also works for
starting a new character with a name other than your account name.

